    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d136">

                <pb facs="0429" n="413" sameAs="frus:frus1950v01/pg413"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">Policy Planning Staff Files</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Memorandum by the Special Assistant for
                        Intelligence</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Armstrong</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State and the Under Secretary of
                        State</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Webb</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">top secret</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1950-11-17">November 17, 1950</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p rendition="#flush">Subject: National Intelligence Estimate No. 3: Soviet
                    Capabilities and Intentions.</p>
                <p>This national estimate is a condensation of the estimate prepared by the US and
                    UK intelligence teams last month, with only two changes of substance. These
                    changes are additions (page 2, para. 10; page 23, para. 63, third and following
                    sentences) based upon General Smith’s statement to the NSC stemming from the
                    Korean situation;<anchor n="1" xml:id="d136-f1"/> they embody no significant
                    departure from the US–UK estimate.</p>
                <p>It is the intention of General Smith, with the Intelligence Advisory Committee,
                    to keep this estimate under continual review as well as to prepare particular
                    estimates bearing on immediate situations, both general and local, which have a
                    bearing on the over-all intentions and capabilities.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">W. Park Armstrong, Jr</hi>.</signed>
                </closer>



                <xi:include href="d136-a1.xml" xpointer="d136-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d136-f1" n="1" xml:id="d136-f1-content">
                <p>For text of the statement under reference, presented by Walter Bedell Smith,
                    Director of the Central Intelligence Agency, at the 71st Meeting of the National
                    Security Council, November 9, see <ref target="frus1950v07#pg_1122">vol. <hi
                            rendition="#small-caps">vii</hi>, p. 1122</ref>.</p>
            </note>
